{title: Be Still and Know}
{subtitle: Psalm 46}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 118}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [B] | [B] |
| [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Though the earth gives way beneath us and [F#]the mountains start to fall
[C#]Down into the heart of the sea, [D#m]we will not fear at all
Let the waters roar and foam and the [F#]hills shake at their swell
We have [C#]found a stronger shelter than the [D#m]walls in which we dwell
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
God is our re[F#]fuge and strength
[C#]A help in troubles, [G#]always to be [D#m]found
The LORD of hosts [F#]is with us
[C#]The God of Jacob [G#]is our for[D#m]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
There's a river in the city and its [F#]streams run clear and wide
God is [C#]in her midst, she will not be shaken, [D#m]he is at her side
Nations rage and kingdoms totter, at [F#]his voice the earth melts down
He breaks [C#]the bow and shatters spears and burns the char[D#m]iots to the ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
God is our re[F#]fuge and strength
[C#]A help in troubles, [G#]always to be [D#m]found
The LORD of hosts [F#]is with us
[C#]The God of Jacob [G#]is our for[B]tress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Be [D#m]still, and know that I am [B]God
I will [F#]be exalted among the na[C#]tions
I will [B]be exalted in the [D#m]earth
Be [C#]still, and know that I am [D#m]God
{end_of_bridge}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [B] | [B] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [C#] | [C#] | ×2
| [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
God is our re[F#]fuge and strength
[C#]A help in troubles, [G#m]always to be [D#m]found
The LORD of hosts [F#]is with us
[C#]The God of Jacob is [G#m]our fortress
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Be [D#m]still, and know that [C#]I am God
[G#m]The LORD of hosts is with [D#m]us
{end_of_verse}

